(1,0,1,'Board rules - READ THIS FIRST','Dave','dave@davespage.geocities.com','http://www.geocities.com/SiliconValley/4423/','Welcome to my board. A few rules:\n\n1. No flaming. If you disagree, say why.\n2. No ALL CAPS subjects.\n3. Do not post other people''s e-mail addresses.\n4. Anything off topic goes in the last thread, not a new one.\n\nThat is it. Have fun. -- Dave',UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-432000,UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-180000,'24.3.14.201'),
(2,1,1,'Re: Board rules - READ THIS FIRST','Webmaster','dave@davespage.geocities.com','','Bumping this because nobody reads it.',UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-180000,0,'24.3.14.201'),
(3,0,3,'Anyone got Half-Life to run on a P200?','Dave','dave@davespage.geocities.com','','I have a P200 MMX with 32mb and a Matrox Mystique. It runs but it is a slideshow in the big rooms. Do I need a 3d card or more RAM first?\n\nSoftware mode looks terrible either way.',UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-259200,UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-198000,'24.3.14.201'),
(4,3,3,'Re: Anyone got Half-Life to run on a P200?','jeff','jeff@netcom.com','','RAM first. 32mb is not enough for Win95 plus HL. I went to 64mb and it stopped hitting the swap file constantly.\n\nThen get a Voodoo2. Night and day.',UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-250000,0,'206.14.9.77'),
(5,4,3,'Re: Anyone got Half-Life to run on a P200?','Dave','dave@davespage.geocities.com','','Thanks. 64mb is $85 at the computer show this weekend so I will start there.',UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-244000,0,'24.3.14.201'),
(6,5,3,'Re: Anyone got Half-Life to run on a P200?','jeff','jeff@netcom.com','','[quote]64mb is $85[/quote]\n\nThat is a fair price right now. Check it is PC100 and not PC66 or you will be back next year.',UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-240000,0,'206.14.9.77'),
(7,3,3,'Re: Anyone got Half-Life to run on a P200?','kewl_dude','kewl_dude@hotmail.com','http://members.aol.com/kewldude98/','GET A VOODOO2!!! [b]12mb[/b] one. my frame rate went from like 15 to 45',UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-201000,0,'152.163.199.44'),
(8,7,3,'Re: Anyone got Half-Life to run on a P200?','hardware_hank','hank@ix.netcom.com','','Two 12mb ones in SLI if you have the slots. Overkill for a P200 though, the CPU will hold you back long before the card does.',UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-198000,0,'199.182.120.3'),
(9,0,9,'MY SITE IS UP!!! PLEASE SIGN GUESTBOOK','kewl_dude','kewl_dude@hotmail.com','http://members.aol.com/kewldude98/','MY HOMEPAGE IS FINALLY UP!!! PLEASE GO SIGN MY GUESTBOOK I WILL SIGN YOURS BACK\n\n[url]http://members.aol.com/kewldude98/[/url]\n\nit has midi',UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-190000,UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-150000,'152.163.199.44'),
(10,9,9,'Re: MY SITE IS UP!!! PLEASE SIGN GUESTBOOK','Webmaster','dave@davespage.geocities.com','','Please do not use all caps in subject lines. See rule 2. Leaving this one up.',UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-188000,0,'24.3.14.201'),
(11,10,9,'Re: MY SITE IS UP!!! PLEASE SIGN GUESTBOOK','kewl_dude','kewl_dude@hotmail.com','','sorry. caps lock was stuck',UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-186000,0,'152.163.199.44'),
(12,9,9,'Re: MY SITE IS UP!!! PLEASE SIGN GUESTBOOK','sk8ter_girl','','','i signed it. the midi is loud but the page is cool. mine is in my profile',UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-150000,0,'207.69.200.12'),
(13,0,13,'Is anyone else worried about Y2K??','wendy_h','wendy_h@juno.com','','My bank sent a letter saying they are compliant but my husband says the power company is the one to worry about. We bought bottled water and a generator.\n\nAm I being silly? It is only 15 months away now.',UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-172800,UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-88000,'209.240.201.9'),
(14,13,13,'Re: Is anyone else worried about Y2K??','y2k_prepper','','','You are not being silly. Get cash out in December 1999 too, the ATMs are the weak link. I have 6 months of food.',UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-170000,0,'198.81.129.100'),
(15,13,13,'Re: Is anyone else worried about Y2K??','jeff','jeff@netcom.com','','I work on mainframes. The date fix has been going on for three years and most of the big systems are done. The small stuff will break for a week and get patched.\n\nWater is fine. A generator is a lot of money for a long weekend.',UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-120000,0,'206.14.9.77'),
(16,15,13,'Re: Is anyone else worried about Y2K??','wendy_h','wendy_h@juno.com','','[quote]The small stuff will break for a week and get patched.[/quote]\n\nThat is reassuring, thank you. I am keeping the water.',UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-90000,0,'209.240.201.9'),
(17,15,13,'Re: Is anyone else worried about Y2K??','y2k_prepper','','','Ask me again on January 3rd.',UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-88000,0,'198.81.129.100'),
(18,0,18,'Geocities or Tripod - which is better?','newbie99','newbie99@hotmail.com','','I want to put up a page about my band. Which free host should I use? I have heard Geocities puts a big watermark on everything now.',UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-140000,UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-96000,'63.12.44.8'),
(19,18,18,'Re: Geocities or Tripod - which is better?','sk8ter_girl','','','Angelfire. 5 megs and the ad is at the bottom not floating over the page.',UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-139000,0,'207.69.200.12'),
(20,18,18,'Re: Geocities or Tripod - which is better?','Dave','dave@davespage.geocities.com','','I am on Geocities and the floating watermark is annoying but 11 megs is hard to beat. Tripod compresses your images which killed my scans.',UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-100000,0,'24.3.14.201'),
(21,19,18,'Re: Geocities or Tripod - which is better?','newbie99','newbie99@hotmail.com','','Went with Angelfire. Thanks both.',UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-96000,0,'63.12.44.8'),
(22,0,22,'FS: Voodoo2 12MB - $89 shipped','hardware_hank','hank@ix.netcom.com','','Diamond Monster 3D II, 12mb, box and drivers. Works perfect, I am going to a Voodoo3.\n\n$89 shipped CONUS. Money order only, no checks. E-mail me.',UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-95000,UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-60000,'199.182.120.3'),
(23,22,22,'Re: FS: Voodoo2 12MB - $89 shipped','kewl_dude','kewl_dude@hotmail.com','','is it still available????',UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-72000,0,'152.163.199.44'),
(24,23,22,'Re: FS: Voodoo2 12MB - $89 shipped','hardware_hank','hank@ix.netcom.com','','SOLD, thanks all. Please do not e-mail any more.',UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-60000,0,'199.182.120.3'),
(25,0,25,'Netscape 4.5 or IE4 - which do you use?','browserwars','','','Serious question, not a flame. I have been on Netscape since 2.0 but 4.5 crashes on me twice a day. IE4 is faster but it puts junk all over my desktop.\n\nWhat is everyone running?',UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-86000,UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-40000,'128.113.24.55'),
(26,25,25,'Re: Netscape 4.5 or IE4 - which do you use?','jeff','jeff@netcom.com','','Netscape 4.5 here. It leaks memory badly, just restart it at lunch.',UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-80000,0,'206.14.9.77'),
(27,25,25,'Re: Netscape 4.5 or IE4 - which do you use?','Dave','dave@davespage.geocities.com','','IE4 at work because it is what is installed, Netscape at home. This board works in both, I test it.',UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-75000,0,'24.3.14.201'),
(28,27,25,'Re: Netscape 4.5 or IE4 - which do you use?','browserwars','','','[b]That[/b] is the real answer isn''t it. Nobody can pick one so we all run both.',UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-70000,0,'128.113.24.55'),
(29,25,25,'Re: Netscape 4.5 or IE4 - which do you use?','sk8ter_girl','','','opera. its 1.5 megs and it doesnt crash',UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-40000,0,'207.69.200.12'),
(30,0,30,'How do I get MP3s off my CDs?','mp3newbie','','','I keep reading about MP3 but I do not understand how you get the songs off the CD. Is there a program? My CD-ROM is a 24x Creative.',UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-70000,UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-50000,'166.72.14.90'),
(31,30,30,'Re: How do I get MP3s off my CDs?','hardware_hank','hank@ix.netcom.com','','Rip with WinDAC to a WAV, then encode with the Xing encoder. Or get AudioCatalyst which does both in one step.\n\nOne song is about 3.5mb at 128kbps. A whole CD takes about 20 minutes on a machine like yours.',UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-65000,0,'199.182.120.3'),
(32,31,30,'Re: How do I get MP3s off my CDs?','mp3newbie','','','Got it working. 20 minutes was optimistic on mine, more like an hour.',UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-62000,0,'166.72.14.90'),
(33,30,30,'Re: How do I get MP3s off my CDs?','kewl_dude','kewl_dude@hotmail.com','','then get [b]winamp[/b] to play them. it really whips the llamas ass',UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-50000,0,'152.163.199.44'),
(34,0,34,'STAR WARS EPISODE 1 TRAILER IS OUT (56k warning)','Dave','dave@davespage.geocities.com','','It is up on the Apple site in QuickTime. 25 megs for the big one.\n\nDo not try this on a 28.8. I started it before dinner and it was still going when I got back.',UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-45000,UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-12000,'24.3.14.201'),
(35,34,34,'Re: STAR WARS EPISODE 1 TRAILER IS OUT (56k warning)','newbie99','newbie99@hotmail.com','','40 minutes on my 56k and it dropped at 90%. Starting again.',UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-30000,0,'63.12.44.8'),
(36,35,34,'Re: STAR WARS EPISODE 1 TRAILER IS OUT (56k warning)','jeff','jeff@netcom.com','','Use a download manager that resumes. GetRight will pick up where it dropped.',UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-28000,0,'206.14.9.77'),
(37,34,34,'Re: STAR WARS EPISODE 1 TRAILER IS OUT (56k warning)','wendy_h','wendy_h@juno.com','','Worth the wait. My son has watched it nine times.',UNIX_TIMESTAMP()-12000,0,'209.240.201.9'),
